course: dictionary
lesson: 5939
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which meaning the writer means. Look at the clues first. A small-letter «mason» is a person who works with stone or brick. A capital-letter Mason is often a name or a member of a club.
explain: «A mason repairs the stone walls of the old garden.» The clues are repairs, stone walls and garden, so a mason is a person who works with stone. Check it: put the meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. Long ago, masons built castles and cathedrals by hand.
explain: «Picture Mason at Grandad's hospital bed.» Here Mason has a capital letter and is a person's name, because a boy hiding behind his mum is not doing stonework. Capital letters and the clues in the rest of the sentence help you tell a job from a name.
explain: Do not stop at the first meaning you know. Ask whether it fits the sentence, and if it does not, try another meaning until one does.
fact: A mason is a person who builds or works with stone or bricks.
fact: A mason is also called a stonemason or bricklayer.
fact: A Mason with a capital M can be a member of a secret social club called the Freemasons.
fact: Mason is also a first name and a family name.
fact: A Mason jar is a glass jar, a name used in the USA.
exercise: «A mason repairs the stone walls of the old garden.» What is a mason? | A kind of garden tool | *A person who builds or works with stone or bricks | A member of a secret club only | A glass jar for jam
exercise: Dad says, «Pass me the Mason jar, please.» In the USA, what is a Mason jar? | *A glass jar | A stone wall | A secret club | A bee hotel
exercise: «A red mason bee fills each stem with rooms and walls them off with mud.» What does mason suggest about the bee? | It flies very fast | *It builds walls, like a stone worker | It reads the newspaper | It sings loudly at night
test: «The master mason checked each stone before it went on the castle wall.» What is a master mason? | A bee that builds with mud | *A stone worker who is in charge of the building work | A cook who works in a castle | A glass jar used for storing jam
test: Ruby met Mason at school, and he told her his surname was Mason. What is Mason here? | *A name | A glass jar | A job that builds with stone | A secret club
exam: «He is a Mason and goes to the club meeting each Tuesday.» What is a Mason here? | A person who builds with stone | *A member of a secret social club called the Freemasons | A first name only | A glass jar
